---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

/* Every number on this page comes from the 30 Sep 2026 measurement of the
 * production database (read-only counts). Update the numbers and AS_OF
 * together, never one without the other. */
const AS_OF = 'September 30, 2026';
const AS_OF_ISO = '2026-09-30';
---

<Layout
  title="What's in VOLI: NCAA, MLV & LOVB Coverage"
  description="18,000+ matches played since 2023, nearly 480,000 NCAA player box scores, play-by-play, and 18,000+ honors back to 1979. All in the free VOLI app."
  activePage="coverage"
  ogUrl="https://playvoli.com/coverage"
  schema={{
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "WebPage",
    "@id": "https://playvoli.com/coverage#webpage",
    "url": "https://playvoli.com/coverage",
    "name": "What's in VOLI",
    "dateModified": AS_OF_ISO,
    "isPartOf": { "@id": "https://playvoli.com/#website" },
    "about": { "@id": "https://playvoli.com/#app" }
  }}
>
  <main class="page">
    <article class="card">
      <p class="eyebrow">Coverage</p>
      <h1>What's in VOLI</h1>
      <p class="lead">Follow a match live, look up any player, or go back through the history of the sport. Here's what's inside the free VOLI app, as of September 2026.</p>
      <p class="lead" style="margin-top:0.75rem">Fantasy, live games, box scores, play-by-play, the VOLI Top 100, the Volleyball Encyclopedia, news and podcasts, all in one app, for NCAA Division I women's volleyball, Major League Volleyball (MLV) and LOVB.</p>
      <p class="asof">Numbers as of <time datetime={AS_OF_ISO}>{AS_OF}</time>.</p>

      <section class="block" id="fantasy">
        <h2>Fantasy volleyball <span class="tag">Play with friends</span></h2>
        <p>Build a team from real college or pro players and play the season against your friends, in a public league, a private one, or a league run by your favorite volleyball podcast. Fantasy runs on salary caps and multi-round contracts, with trades and a signing window between rounds, and it is scored from the same box scores you see everywhere else in VOLI.</p>
        <div class="stats">
          <div class="stat"><b>227</b><span>fantasy leagues</span></div>
          <div class="stat"><b>1,375</b><span>managers</span></div>
          <div class="stat"><b>2,068</b><span>fantasy teams</span></div>
          <div class="stat"><b>105,593</b><span>contracts signed</span></div>
        </div>
        <p class="limits"><strong>Since:</strong> MLV fantasy since December 2025; NCAA Division I women's fantasy since August 2026. <strong>Limits:</strong> fantasy covers NCAA Division I women's volleyball and MLV. Fantasy is optional: everything else in VOLI works without it.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="block" id="leagues">
        <h2>Leagues and seasons</h2>
        <p>Choose a league, a season and a team, and VOLI has the schedule, the results and the roster.</p>
        <div class="table-wrap">
          <table>
            <caption>Leagues with match-by-match data in VOLI</caption>
            <thead><tr><th>League</th><th>First season</th><th class="num">Matches on file</th><th class="num">Teams</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td>NCAA Division I women's</td><td>2023</td><td class="num">20,173</td><td class="num">405 programs, 33 conferences</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Major League Volleyball (MLV)</td><td>2024 (as the Pro Volleyball Federation)</td><td class="num">319</td><td class="num">13 clubs</td></tr>
              <tr><td>LOVB Pro</td><td>2025</td><td class="num">126</td><td class="num">10 clubs</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <div class="stats">
          <div class="stat"><b>18,082</b><span>matches played since August 2023</span></div>
          <div class="stat"><b>11,821</b><span>player profiles</span></div>
          <div class="stat"><b>6,282</b><span>NCAA players on 2026 rosters (364 teams)</span></div>
          <div class="stat"><b>952</b><span>pro transactions logged since 2023</span></div>
        </div>
        <p class="limits"><strong>Earliest:</strong> NCAA August 2023, MLV January 2024, LOVB January 2025. <strong>Limits:</strong> Athletes Unlimited appears in the history archive (honors 2021–2025), not in live games. Matches on file include the rest of the 2026 NCAA schedule through November 28.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="block" id="box-scores">
        <h2>Box scores and player stats</h2>
        <p>Open any player and see their game log, season totals and per-set rates; sort the leaderboards by season, conference, position and class.</p>
        <div class="stats">
          <div class="stat"><b>479,626</b><span>NCAA player box scores (one per player per match)</span></div>
          <div class="stat"><b>99.8%</b><span>of completed Division I matches since 2023 have a box score</span></div>
          <div class="stat"><b>445 of 445</b><span>MLV and LOVB matches with set-by-set player stats</span></div>
          <div class="stat"><b>17,568</b><span>NCAA match MVPs named by VOLI</span></div>
        </div>
        <p>For pro matches VOLI keeps 31,038 per-set player stat records (30+ fields, including reception, dig and set quality) and 30,754 graded per-set records that split attack, serve, receive, block, dig, set and freeball into positive, negative and error.</p>
        <p class="limits"><strong>Earliest:</strong> NCAA 2023, pro 2024. <strong>Limits:</strong> 100% of the 2025 and 2026 seasons and of all NCAA Tournament matches since 2023; 2023 and 2024 are just under 100%. Per-match stats start in 2023, so earlier years are covered through honors, polls, results and record books rather than box scores. Match MVPs are NCAA only.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="block" id="play-by-play">
        <h2>Play-by-play and live</h2>
        <p>Follow a match point by point: each rally, substitution and rotation, a lead chart for each set, and the score on your lock screen. <a class="inline" href="/game-center">See a real match</a>.</p>
        <div class="stats">
          <div class="stat"><b>360,723</b><span>NCAA rallies logged in the 2026 season</span></div>
          <div class="stat"><b>119,180</b><span>NCAA substitutions logged in 2026</span></div>
          <div class="stat"><b>41,241</b><span>pro play-by-play events, 445 matches</span></div>
          <div class="stat"><b>438,155</b><span>point-by-point score states behind the lead charts</span></div>
        </div>
        <p>Live matches update in the app as they are played. On iPhone, Live Activities put the scoreboard on the lock screen and in the Dynamic Island, and a home-screen widget shows the next game.</p>
        <p class="limits"><strong>Earliest:</strong> pro play-by-play 2024; NCAA play-by-play 2026 season (2,259 matches so far). <strong>Limits:</strong> 2023–2025 NCAA matches have box scores but not play-by-play.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="block" id="rankings">
        <h2>Rankings and chance to win</h2>
        <p>See where your team stands and who is likely to win before first serve.</p>
        <div class="stats">
          <div class="stat"><b>Top 100</b><span>VOLI's own Division I ranking, published each Monday</span></div>
          <div class="stat"><b>25,401</b><span>team rating snapshots, 2023–2026</span></div>
          <div class="stat"><b>3,330</b><span>college matches with a pre-match chance to win</span></div>
          <div class="stat"><b>666</b><span>AVCA Coaches Polls in the archive, since 1982</span></div>
        </div>
        <p>VOLI rates every Division I team from match results and strength of schedule. Each upcoming college match shows each team's chance to win and the most likely set score. <a class="inline" href="/methods">How it works</a>.</p>
        <p class="limits"><strong>Earliest:</strong> the Top 100 has been published each Monday since September 2026; ratings were computed afterwards for 2023–2025 with the same model. Match predictions since September 2026. <strong>Limits:</strong> Division I women's only; no in-match win probability.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="block" id="encyclopedia">
        <h2>The Volleyball Encyclopedia</h2>
        <p>Was your school ever national champion? Who were the All-Americans the year you graduated? Look it up.</p>
        <div class="stats">
          <div class="stat"><b>18,319</b><span>honors, about 5,140 honorees, back to 1979</span></div>
          <div class="stat"><b>3,019</b><span>AVCA All-America selections since 1981</span></div>
          <div class="stat"><b>45</b><span>NCAA champions, 1981–2025</span></div>
          <div class="stat"><b>15,969</b><span>ranked entries across 666 AVCA polls</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="table-wrap">
          <table>
            <caption>Volumes in the Volleyball Encyclopedia</caption>
            <thead><tr><th>Volume</th><th class="num">Entries</th><th>Years</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td>AVCA national honors (All-America, Player and Coach of the Year, Player of the Week)</td><td class="num">3,590</td><td>1981–2025</td></tr>
              <tr><td>AVCA regional honors (All-Region and regional awards)</td><td class="num">5,824</td><td>1986–2025</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Conference honors: ACC, Big 12, Big Ten, SEC</td><td class="num">8,584</td><td>1979–2025</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Pro honors: MLV, LOVB, Athletes Unlimited</td><td class="num">321</td><td>2021–2026</td></tr>
              <tr><td>AVCA Coaches Poll (weekly, preseason and final)</td><td class="num">666 polls</td><td>1982–2026</td></tr>
              <tr><td>NCAA champions and conference champions</td><td class="num">312</td><td>1979–2025</td></tr>
              <tr><td>NCAA record book (individual and team)</td><td class="num">3,130</td><td>1981–2025</td></tr>
              <tr><td>MLV and LOVB record books</td><td class="num">2,012</td><td>2024–2026</td></tr>
              <tr><td>MLV Draft selections</td><td class="num">107</td><td>2024–2026</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Conference membership, year by year</td><td class="num">13,178 team-years</td><td>1981–2026</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="limits"><strong>Earliest:</strong> 1979 (SEC honors and conference tournaments). <strong>Limits:</strong> history, not per-match stats, before 2023. Conference honors cover four conferences. All-America lists hold the first team only in 1981 and the first and second teams in 1984–2001; 2019 is partial, and the 2020 season, played in spring 2021, is filed under 2021.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="block" id="news-and-podcasts">
        <h2>News and podcasts</h2>
        <p>Read the latest volleyball stories and listen to volleyball podcasts without leaving the app. <a class="inline" href="/news-and-podcasts">More on reading and listening</a>.</p>
        <div class="stats">
          <div class="stat"><b>19</b><span>news outlets, from league and conference sites to independent writers</span></div>
          <div class="stat"><b>1,157</b><span>articles since March 2025</span></div>
          <div class="stat"><b>13</b><span>volleyball podcasts</span></div>
          <div class="stat"><b>884</b><span>episodes, about 751 hours</span></div>
        </div>
        <p class="limits"><strong>Earliest:</strong> news since March 2025; podcast episodes back to 2019. <strong>Limits:</strong> news stories link back to the outlet that published them.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="block" id="community">
        <h2>Play and talk</h2>
        <p>Chat with other fans in a room for each match, team and league; play the Daily Grid, a volleyball trivia grid; and join AMAs with players and creators.</p>
        <div class="stats">
          <div class="stat"><b>2,594</b><span>chat rooms, including one per match</span></div>
          <div class="stat"><b>66</b><span>Daily Grids played since 2025</span></div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <div class="cta">
        <p>VOLI is free on iPhone and Android.</p>
        <div class="cta-row">
          <a class="btn primary" href="https://apps.apple.com/us/app/voli-the-volleyball-hub/id6749812982">Download on the App Store</a>
          <a class="btn" href="https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.playvoli.app">Get it on Google Play</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="related"><a href="/game-center">Follow a match live</a> · <a href="/methods">How VOLI's numbers work</a> · <a href="/news-and-podcasts">News and podcasts</a> · <a href="/faq">FAQ</a></p>
      <p class="fine">VOLI is independent and not affiliated with or endorsed by the NCAA, MLV, LOVB, the AVCA or any conference.</p>
    </article>
  </main>
</Layout>

<style>
    .page {
        width: 100%;
        max-width: 880px;
        margin: 0 auto;
        padding: calc(6rem + env(safe-area-inset-top)) 1rem 3rem;
    }
    .card {
        background: var(--bg-card);
        backdrop-filter: blur(40px);
        -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(40px);
        border: 1px solid var(--glass-border);
        border-radius: 24px;
        padding: 2.75rem 2rem;
        position: relative;
        overflow: hidden;
    }
    .card::before {
        content: '';
        position: absolute;
        top: 0; left: 0; right: 0;
        height: 1px;
        background: linear-gradient(90deg, transparent, var(--glass-highlight), transparent);
    }
    .eyebrow {
        color: var(--accent);
        font-size: 0.75rem;
        font-weight: 600;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        letter-spacing: 0.1em;
        text-align: center;
        margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    }
    h1 {
        font-size: 2rem;
        font-weight: 700;
        text-align: center;
        letter-spacing: -0.02em;
        margin-bottom: 1rem;
    }
    .lead {
        color: var(--text-secondary);
        font-size: 1.05rem;
        line-height: 1.75;
        text-align: center;
        max-width: 640px;
        margin: 0 auto;
    }
    .asof {
        color: var(--text-muted);
        font-size: 0.8rem;
        text-align: center;
        margin-top: 1rem;
    }
    .block { margin-top: 2.75rem; }
    h2 {
        font-size: 1.3rem;
        font-weight: 700;
        letter-spacing: -0.01em;
        margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
    }
    h2 .tag {
        display: inline-block;
        vertical-align: middle;
        margin-left: 0.5rem;
        padding: 0.15rem 0.55rem;
        border-radius: 100px;
        background: var(--accent-subtle);
        color: var(--accent);
        font-size: 0.65rem;
        font-weight: 600;
        letter-spacing: 0.04em;
        text-transform: uppercase;
    }
    h3 {
        font-size: 1rem;
        font-weight: 600;
        margin: 1.25rem 0 0.5rem;
    }
    p, li {
        color: var(--text-secondary);
        font-size: 0.97rem;
        line-height: 1.75;
    }
    p + p { margin-top: 0.75rem; }
    ul.plain { padding-left: 1.15rem; }
    ul.plain li { margin-bottom: 0.35rem; }
    strong { color: var(--text-primary); font-weight: 600; }
    a.inline { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
    .limits {
        margin-top: 0.75rem;
        padding: 0.7rem 0.9rem;
        border-left: 2px solid var(--electric-blue);
        background: rgba(0, 212, 255, 0.05);
        border-radius: 0 10px 10px 0;
        color: var(--text-muted);
        font-size: 0.85rem;
        line-height: 1.6;
    }
    .limits strong { color: var(--text-secondary); }
    .stats {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(170px, 1fr));
        gap: 0.6rem;
        margin: 1rem 0 0.25rem;
    }
    .stat {
        padding: 0.9rem 1rem;
        background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03);
        border: 1px solid var(--glass-border);
        border-radius: 14px;
    }
    .stat b {
        display: block;
        color: var(--text-primary);
        font-size: 1.35rem;
        font-weight: 700;
        letter-spacing: -0.01em;
        font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    }
    .stat span {
        color: var(--text-muted);
        font-size: 0.8rem;
        line-height: 1.4;
    }
    .table-wrap {
        overflow-x: auto;
        -webkit-overflow-scrolling: touch;
        margin-top: 0.75rem;
        border: 1px solid var(--glass-border);
        border-radius: 14px;
    }
    table {
        width: 100%;
        border-collapse: collapse;
        font-size: 0.88rem;
        font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    }
    caption {
        caption-side: top;
        text-align: left;
        padding: 0.7rem 0.9rem 0.3rem;
        color: var(--text-muted);
        font-size: 0.78rem;
    }
    th, td {
        padding: 0.55rem 0.8rem;
        text-align: left;
        border-bottom: 1px solid var(--glass-border);
        white-space: nowrap;
    }
    th {
        color: var(--text-muted);
        font-weight: 600;
        font-size: 0.72rem;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    }
    td { color: var(--text-secondary); }
    td.num, th.num { text-align: right; }
    tr:last-child td { border-bottom: none; }
    tr.total td { color: var(--text-primary); font-weight: 600; background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.02); }
    td.win { color: var(--accent); font-weight: 700; }
    .cta {
        margin-top: 3rem;
        padding: 1.5rem;
        text-align: center;
        background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03);
        border: 1px solid var(--glass-border);
        border-radius: 18px;
    }
    .cta p { margin-bottom: 1rem; }
    .cta-row { display: flex; gap: 0.6rem; justify-content: center; flex-wrap: wrap; }
    .btn {
        display: inline-flex;
        align-items: center;
        padding: 0.7rem 1.2rem;
        border-radius: 100px;
        font-size: 0.9rem;
        font-weight: 600;
        border: 1px solid var(--glass-border);
        background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.04);
        color: var(--text-primary);
        transition: background 0.2s;
    }
    .btn:hover { background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); }
    .btn.primary { background: var(--accent); color: #000; border-color: var(--accent); }
    .btn.primary:hover { background: #d4ff33; }
    .related { margin-top: 1.5rem; text-align: center; font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--text-muted); }
    .related a { color: var(--text-secondary); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; margin: 0 0.35rem; }
    .fine { color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.8rem; text-align: center; margin-top: 1.5rem; line-height: 1.6; }
    @media (max-width: 480px) {
        .page { padding-left: 1rem; padding-right: 1rem; }
        .card { padding: 2rem 1.1rem; border-radius: 20px; }
        h1 { font-size: 1.6rem; }
        .lead { font-size: 0.98rem; }
        th, td { padding: 0.5rem 0.6rem; }
    }
</style>
